# wheel requires the account password (no NOPASSWD): that password used to be
# the only thing standing between an unlocked lock screen / an SSH session and
# root (security-review.md F1/F6). Checked against the pinned Omarchy Phone
# shell/app revisions (SHELL_REV/APP_REV in build-rootfs.sh): phone-hyprland,
# ophone-sys and the omarchy-phone-session unit never call sudo (they use
# group membership -- wheel/seat/video/input/audio/render -- and
# systemd-logind/polkit for reboot/poweroff/suspend), so this doesn't need a
# narrow NOPASSWD carve-out for anything the phone session does. If a future
# on-phone tool needs one unattended root action, add a line here scoped to
# that exact command, not a blanket rule.
%wheel ALL=(ALL:ALL) ALL
